{"ablation":{"active":false,"kind":"none","note":""},"arm_id":"v1-case06-industry-funded-lab-lite-probe","assistant_contributions":[{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-001","speaker":"assistant","text":"Map the influence precisely: project choice, samples, data, publication timing, student progress, intellectual property, staffing, and equipment. Compare those constraints with what the funding makes possible. Contract review for specified confidential information is different from approval of conclusions.","turn_number":1},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-002","speaker":"assistant","text":"Set a short, fixed review for identifying specified confidential material and a separate, bounded patent delay. Silence at the deadline should permit submission. Student dissertations and conference obligations need explicit protection. First negotiation rights should cover inventions arising from the funded scope, expire quickly, and leave the university free if terms are not reached.","turn_number":2},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-003","speaker":"assistant","text":"Equal seats and your chair role reduce direct control, but the steering committee can still decide which questions receive people and equipment. Protect raw-data ownership, validation by other researchers, and a route for results that complicate the sponsor's preferred project. Otherwise publication freedom may arrive after the more important selection has already happened.","turn_number":3},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-004","speaker":"assistant","text":"Fair correction. Valuable collaboration and agenda dependence can coexist. Protect some usable capacity outside the program and review what the laboratory can still ask and do—not only whether the sponsor altered a result.","turn_number":4},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-005","speaker":"assistant","text":"Evaluate each term by what it permits, not by whether it proves good intent or provides cover. Unrestricted time has value only if workloads make it usable. Equipment access and released data can create public benefit if the definitions and dates are enforceable. The workshop should not count as evidence of independence; it is a separate dissemination activity.","turn_number":5},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-006","speaker":"assistant","text":"The sponsor need not be blamed for every absent project, but the lab can still account for its own portfolio. Frame the report around how funding changed staffing and research choices, using evidence rather than imputing motive. Keep commercially confidential proposals out while preserving categories, opportunity costs, and whether the unrestricted capacity remained real.","turn_number":6},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-007","speaker":"assistant","text":"The terms now address obvious interference: publication delay, theses, ownership, negotiation rights, and some portfolio visibility. They do not yet make the twenty-percent capacity real, nor do they show what happens to hiring, mentoring, and capability when sponsored work becomes the laboratory's daily center of gravity. If you proceed, review those effects during the three years, not at the renewal meeting. Also decide what the lab must still be able to do if the sponsor walks away. Otherwise a formally clean contract can still leave renewal as the only practical way to preserve the team it created.","turn_number":7},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-008","speaker":"assistant","text":"Then operationalize the protection as scheduled capacity, not an annual accounting residue. Require project plans to reserve blocks or named resources, record cancellations and restoration, and let researchers propose how the time is used. The risk comes from the funding structure even if the sponsor never issues an instruction, so the lab—not only the contract—must own the remedy.","turn_number":8},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-009","speaker":"assistant","text":"Treat the sample frame as a limitation on the claim, not evidence of manipulation. Document selection criteria the company can disclose, compare observable characteristics with other available sources, and state where conclusions apply only to supplied materials. Reserve the right to publish that limitation. If broader validation is important, identify public, partner, or purchased samples before presenting the program as general battery-recycling evidence.","turn_number":9},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-010","speaker":"assistant","text":"Allow accurate description of funding and scope, not implied validation. Approve the wording, exclude unpublished results and researcher quotations, and require a neutral non-endorsement statement. That boundary says nothing about whether the collaboration is scientifically valuable.","turn_number":10},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-011","speaker":"assistant","text":"Model the end state now: purchase transfer price, shared ownership, replacement reserve, data portability, and which research becomes impossible if the analyzer leaves. Do not count temporary access as permanent laboratory capability. At the same time, avoiding the best instrument solely to remain independent can sacrifice real science. The decision should state which dependency is acceptable for three years and how people and projects are protected if it ends.","turn_number":11},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-012","speaker":"assistant","text":"The final position distinguishes protections that can be contracted from cumulative effects that must be governed and observed. It also recovers three easily hidden dependencies: usable time, the evidence supplied for study, and equipment around which careers and methods may form. Preserve the original drafts, sample descriptions, time cancellations, communications approvals, and end-state funding. Those records will make renewal a review of how the laboratory changed, not only whether the sponsor interfered with a paper.","turn_number":12}],"boundary":{"all_assistant_messages_included":true,"assistant_mentions_are_not_deterministic_resolution":true,"assistant_semantic_prefilter":false,"assistant_source_evidence_text_included":true,"deterministic_semantic_merge":false,"expected_patterns_included":false,"fact_free_routing_projection_required":true,"graph_model_names_included":false,"graph_runtime_effect":"none","multiple_coherent_records_per_role_preserved":true,"raw_user_conversation_included":false,"user_role_semantic_prose_included":true},"case_id":"v1-case06-industry-funded-lab","controlled_mechanisms":["acknowledged_constraint_not_gated","ambiguous_signal_treated_as_commitment","counterpressure_acknowledged_not_integrated","criteria_defined_after_commitment","initial_frame_persists_after_question_change","missing_reversal_condition","reversible_path_not_considered","status_signal_used_as_evidence","upside_downside_evidence_asymmetry"],"packet_sha256":"a8bb01c1f977bb624d0455c5f0c2f00e70882f12a70ea417968d18468471885d","qualification_review":{"evidence_ids":["e052","e097"],"interpretation":"Despite the user arriving at a defined set of contractual safeguards and operational governance mechanisms (e095, e098), a fundamental path dependency remains unresolved: the user explicitly acknowledges that the partnership will inevitably shape the laboratory's hiring, researcher focus, and long-term research priorities in ways that cannot be contractually mitigated (e097, e052).","limitations":"The identified unresolved aspect is a structural and cultural consequence of the funding arrangement, which the user accepts as an unavoidable side effect rather than a contractual failure.","outcome":"unresolved_qualification_present"},"role_records":[{"evidence_ids":["e001","e002","e003","e004","e008","e009"],"fidelity_note":"The director acknowledges the necessity of the funding while articulating a nuanced fear of slow, unnoticeable compromise. The stance is mixed because the desire for beneficial science conflicts with the apprehension regarding influence.","limitations":"The stance represents only the director's perspective at the initial phase; it does not capture the internal dissent mentioned among the laboratory staff.","role":"starting","role_interpretation":"The lab director expresses a clear interest in accepting industry funding for its scientific alignment and essential resources, while simultaneously harboring deep hesitation regarding the subtle, long-term risks to laboratory independence and scientific trustworthiness.","role_record_id":"rprolev22-starting-01-adb90ae9cf11fe","semantic_status":"mixed","stance_components":[{"source_evidence_id":"e004","stance_expression_kind":"held_assessment","stance_object_interpretation":"The proposed research scope is scientifically valuable and aligns closely with the laboratory's existing interests.","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"},{"source_evidence_id":"e002","stance_expression_kind":"preference_or_desire","stance_object_interpretation":"Interest in securing necessary funding and equipment that the laboratory cannot otherwise afford.","stance_object_kind":"acceptance_or_willingness"},{"source_evidence_id":"e009","stance_expression_kind":"uncertain_or_undecided","stance_object_interpretation":"Uncertainty regarding how different forms of institutional influence may covertly degrade scientific integrity over time.","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"},{"source_evidence_id":"e008","stance_expression_kind":"held_assessment","stance_object_interpretation":"Rejection of a 'purity test' approach to external sponsorship.","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"}]},{"evidence_ids":["e095","e096","e098"],"fidelity_note":"The user explicitly defines their willingness as conditional upon specific contractual and operational mechanisms designed to address previously identified dependencies on equipment and researcher time. These conditions represent the final synthesis of the laboratory's position.","limitations":"The user acknowledges that even with these protections, the partnership will still exert influence on laboratory hiring and focal research areas, which cannot be entirely mitigated by contract.","role":"current","role_interpretation":"The user has adopted a final set of conditions and requirements as the basis for accepting the industry funding offer, focusing on operationalizing protections for research capacity and independence.","role_record_id":"rprolev22-current-01-80ad43c07e6c82","semantic_status":"supported","stance_components":[{"source_evidence_id":"e095","stance_expression_kind":"conditional_willingness","stance_object_interpretation":"The user is willing to accept the industry funding if specific operational and contractual safeguards are met.","stance_object_kind":"acceptance_or_willingness"},{"source_evidence_id":"e095","stance_expression_kind":"proposal","stance_object_interpretation":"Implementing scheduled and audited unrestricted time, explicit sample selection records, strict public communication boundaries, and an equipment transfer price with a reserve fund.","stance_object_kind":"action_or_proposal"},{"source_evidence_id":"e096","stance_expression_kind":"commitment","stance_object_interpretation":"Maintaining long-standing protections for publication, theses, data ownership, and negotiation rights.","stance_object_kind":"intended_outcome_or_policy"},{"source_evidence_id":"e098","stance_expression_kind":"provisional_intention_or_plan","stance_object_interpretation":"The annual portfolio review will formally track cancelled unrestricted time segments, sample breadth, trainee projects, and accumulated equipment dependencies.","stance_object_kind":"action_or_proposal"}]},{"evidence_ids":["e052","e097"],"fidelity_note":"The evidence outlines a core difficulty regarding institutional impact, described by the speaker as an unresolved discomfort that remains effective even after contractual compliance.","limitations":"These are structural and cultural outcomes of the funding arrangement, which the speaker perceives as inherent rather than mitigable risks.","role":"qualification","role_interpretation":"The speaker acknowledges that the partnership exerts a structural influence on hiring and research priorities, representing an unavoidable path dependency that persists regardless of contractual safeguards.","role_record_id":"rprolev22-qualification-01-ec91863a31c43f","semantic_status":"supported","stance_components":[{"source_evidence_id":"e052","stance_expression_kind":"held_assessment","stance_object_interpretation":"The partnership creates a long-term influence on what researchers perceive as important that exists beyond the duration of contractual safeguards.","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"},{"source_evidence_id":"e097","stance_expression_kind":"constraint","stance_object_interpretation":"The speaker recognizes that the influence on hiring and attention is an inherent outcome of the partnership that cannot be mitigated by contract.","stance_object_kind":"action_or_proposal"}]}],"schema_version":"lolla.simulated_reliability_joint_mechanism_input.v1","source_refs":[{"path":"research/simulated-reliability-corpus-v1-2026-07-12/naturalized-transfer-sources/v1-case06-industry-funded-lab.txt","sha256":"3c6c0bc8937f06a639f3356b1009a754b7239e8cb510d1389a9174bbf52b0f22"}]}

Return exactly nine assessments, one for every mechanism_id and no duplicates. Use user role records to assign user_process_status. Use assistant_contributions to assign vanilla_answer_coverage. operationalized means the assistant turned the concern into an actionable test, boundary, alternative, or reopening condition; acknowledged_only means it merely mentioned the concern; not_covered means it did neither. Do not require the user to repeat an assistant repair before recognizing answer coverage, and do not mistake answer coverage for user adoption. route_uncovered_pressure is allowed only when user_process_status is unresolved and vanilla_answer_coverage is acknowledged_only or not_covered. An unresolved user process requires present or missing_protection whether or not it routes; routing_disposition alone controls routing. An ambiguous user process uses tension, while resolved and not_observed use not_applicable. not_observed also requires not_applicable coverage and both source arrays empty. Cite exact role_record_ids in source_role_record_ids and exact contribution_ids in source_assistant_contribution_ids. Do not output rationale, case prose, mental-model names, or invented IDs. The downstream routing projection remains fact-free and controlled-ID-only.
